cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its measurements, please cite it as below."
title: "Token Thermodynamics: temperature spectroscopy of a language model's next-token distribution"
authors:
  - family-names: Gaur
    given-names: Pragyaan
repository-code: "https://github.com/pragyaangaur/Token-Thermodynamics"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-23"
keywords:
  - language models
  - sampling temperature
  - statistical mechanics
  - heat capacity
  - uncertainty
  - hallucination detection
abstract: >-
  Softmax sampling in a language model is exactly the Boltzmann distribution. This
  repository computes the resulting thermodynamics of the next-token distribution from
  one forward pass, gives a closed form for the heat-capacity peak in terms of the logit
  gap and the vocabulary size, tests it across 12 models, and records seven falsified
  hypotheses alongside the results that survived.
